"A few days later the report of his defeat was heard. The Emperor found no savor in his food and no pleasure in holding court; the great ministers were anxious and afraid and did not know what to do.": "2b5cc03f47e2",
"A fierce tiger in the deep hills makes every beast tremble; but once in a cage or a pit it wags its tail and begs for food. Restraint works upon it by degrees.": "a2f718a46fc3",
"A letter cannot say all that is meant. I have set out my poor and narrow thoughts. Respectfully, I bow twice.": "51ecc954ab08",
"A man has but one death. It may be heavier than Mount T'ai or lighter than a goose feather: it depends on what he uses it for.": "07f194fad5ff",
"A man who cannot make an end of himself early, while still outside the reach of the law, but slides down by degrees until he is among the whips and rods, and only then wishes to die for his honor — is he not far from it?": "6403038b7d9f",
"A man who has undergone that punishment is not reckoned among men — and this is not the way of one age only; it comes down from far back.": "b66b1a77df36",
"Alas, alas! What has a man like me left to say? What is there left to say?": "2e33ed3b34a0",
"All these men had something knotted up inside them; they could not get their way through, and so they set down what was past, thinking of those who would come.": "0d88774c470d",
"All these men rose to be kings, marquises, generals and chancellors, and their names were heard in neighboring states; yet when guilt came and the net fell on them they could not make an end of themselves, but lay in the dust. It has been one and the same from ancient times until now. Where among them is the man who was not disgraced?": "8cc03f2a4cd9",
"All this you saw for yourself, Shao-ch'ing. Was it not so with me?": "a6977b4bf6e6",
"And for a man who has come to this to say that he is not disgraced is merely brazening it out.": "0bdeb0487d58",
"And for a man who has come to this to say that he is not disgraced is merely brazening it out. What is there in that worth valuing?": "6e36fb2989c8",
"And now you instruct me to recommend the worthy and advance scholars. Is that not at cross purposes with what is in my heart?": "23b9a6925a6c",
"And so my bowels turn nine times in a day; at home I am dazed as though I had lost something; going out, I do not know where I am going.": "88a32522f281",
"And the world would not even rank me with those who die for principle; it would merely say my wits were exhausted and my guilt complete, that I could not save myself and so went to my death. Why? Because of what I had made of myself all along.": "1f59964de8df",
"At the lowest, I could not pile up days and accumulate service, take high office and a fat salary, and bring glory to my clan and my friends.": "7232ebbee57f",
"Before Ling went under, a messenger came with word of him, and the high ministers, princes and nobles of Han all raised their cups to drink his health.": "f4277a360ab6",
"Being nothing but a servant of the inner chambers, how could I withdraw and hide deep among the cliffs and caves? So I drift with the crowd, bend and rise with the times, and let my madness and confusion run their course.": "a12b0ca665dc",
"Besides, it is not easy to live under a stain, and the low ground draws much slander. I met this disaster through words spoken, and became once more a laughingstock to my village, disgracing my forebears. With what face could I go up again to my parents' grave mound?": "e1d619bac0ba",
"Besides, the brave do not necessarily die for principle, and a coward who longs for duty may make the effort anywhere.": "b7969f9196f6",
"Besides, the whole of this affair is not easy to make plain.": "8e8a703735dd",
"But I consider that my body is maimed and my place unclean: whatever I do draws blame, and trying to help only does harm. So I brood alone — and to whom should I speak?": "3ef6a286c018",
"But my very substance is already broken. Though I carried the jewels of Sui and Ho in my breast and behaved like Hsü Yu and Po I, it could bring me no honor; it would only earn ridicule and stain me further.": "b48bd4f409e9",
"But now, hands and feet bound together, taking the cangue and the rope, the skin laid bare and the rod laid on, shut within round walls —": "74103f04509d",
"But this can be said to the wise; it is hard to say to ordinary men.": "78424933d1e1",
"Chi Pu became a collared slave in the house of Chu Chia; Kuan Fu was disgraced in the guard house.": "fce7e9ff4df8",
